WEBVTT

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.940
What's wrong with him?

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:07.700
It's Tachibana Azuma.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.120
The guy playing with Tonozaki
used to be Mikoto's partner.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.660
He's the reason Mikoto can't
jump backwards anymore.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:22.520
First game won by Tonozaki and Tachibana
from Tomari Transport.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.480
Hey, are you alright?

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.420
I'm fine.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.800
Ain't easy going up against your old partner, eh?

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.600
In the competitive world, only those who win
get to move on to the next round.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:51.140
Are you ready to live in that world, Shiratori?

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.380
We'll win the next game.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.880
Hang in there, Shiratori.
I've staked it all on you.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.440
You can be stronger than this.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:08.300
Second game. Love-all. Play!

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:44.280
[#05: Feedback]

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.580
[#05: Feedback]
Whoa!

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:47.500
They really put them in the paper!

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:50.000
They even called him a "prodigy"!

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:51.500
Are they done yet?

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:53.540
Let's warm up, Azuma.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:55.220
Sure.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.820
It's a real shame Toba High won't sponsor you.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.320
Oh, no, I was expecting it.
Mikoto's a better player than me.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:07.900
What will you do about high school then?

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:09.960
I'll apply to Toba as a regular student.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:13.440
Right. Well, you should have no issue getting in.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:16.260
Hope to see our Golden Pair
keep winning in high school!

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.040
In all honesty, I was panicking.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:27.540
I didn't want him to leave me behind.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:32.960
Time to announce the order.
Doubles 1 will be Shiratori and Tachibana.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:33.820
Yes, sir.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.200
Doubles 2, Saeki and Minaguchi.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:36.940
Yes, sir.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:41.380
He didn't even get a scholarship.
How the hell is he a regular on the team?

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.260
Probably knows the right people.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.840
Alright, assholes,
why don't you say it to his face?

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:48.720
They'd choose you if you played
as good as you run your mouth.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:50.540
Don't listen to them.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.840
We're the strongest together.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:54.120
Yeah.

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:57.860
I wanted a skill of my own.

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:06.620
Wait, you're still here?
I'm locking up, time to go home.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.920
Right, sorry.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:11.340
Go easy on the workout.

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:14.280
You're still growing,
so you better not overdo it.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.020
I'll be careful.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:21.300
I wanted to stand next to Mikoto
and call myself his partner with pride.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:31.360
Yo, isn't that Mitsuhoshi's coach?
Think he's scouting? Now I'm anxious.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:32.380
I'm not.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:37.980
Right, must be nice and easy for you,
being a prodigy and all.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:41.520
Hey! You don't need to be so mean!

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:47.820
On my right, Shiratori and Tachibana
from Toba Daiichi High School.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:51.900
On my left, Kawakami and Kirishima
from Hoyoku High School.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:03.120
You okay, Azuma?

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:07.600
Yeah… Leave the back to me.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:10.080
You just focus on scoring, alright?

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:14.560
They're aiming at me…

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:20.860
I can't keep holding Mikoto back!

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:29.240
I have to make this count!

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:42.460
I was a fool.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:49.500
All I could think of was how
to make myself useful to Mikoto.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:54.760
Second game. Love-all. Play!

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:58.720
None of that was Mikoto's fault.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:08.220
I admired Mikoto.

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:10.080
I wanted to be like him.

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:12.480
But now…

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:15.440
That's the best you can do?!

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:19.220
Is guilt holding you back?

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:31.380
If that's how this game is going to look…

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:34.860
…then I wish we hadn't met again.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:37.640
Oh, he's pissed.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:42.020
It's hard to believe
Tachibana ever injured his biceps!

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:46.140
It's not uncommon for athletes to
give up after getting injured.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:51.820
Not Tachibana though. He slowly clawed
his way out through physical therapy.

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:58.280
He has the strength to pick himself up
and keep fighting even if he falls.

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:00.280
That's why I recruited him in the first place.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:04.620
Not bad for our first game.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:06.380
Thank you.

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:08.840
Time to kick it up a notch.

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:09.860
Think you can keep up?

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:11.120
Yes.

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:19.520
Nice shot!

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:22.860
One more, one more, one more time!

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:25.440
This is bad, they've got them cornered.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:27.460
They're out of sync, too.

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:34.640
Hey. Can't you…

00:07:34.660 --> 00:07:36.140
Can't you get your shit together?!

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:38.140
Are you going easy on me?

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:39.900
Do you feel sorry for me?

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:45.180
You think I'd be happy winning like this?!

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:48.900
Oh no, they're fighting!

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:55.320
Didn't know you could go off like that.

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:59.760
I'm sorry, I spoke out of line.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:13.660
Ow! Crap, I put too much force into that!

00:08:13.940 --> 00:08:15.660
What was that for?!

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:18.160
For you to wake the hell up.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:20.160
Now stop making that face.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:23.120
What are we here to do?

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:25.420
We're here to win.

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:27.060
You got that right.

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:29.800
I've got a plan.

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:33.880
11-2. Play!

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:41.360
Here!

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:42.000
Here!

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:52.560
Shouting, really? At this level?

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:53.400
Yukei.

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:59.200
You're right! It helps them
not only say who'll take the shot

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.580
but also inform each other of their location!

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.460
In other words… muscles!

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:06.960
Talk about basic.

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:11.960
But why now? Aren't you supposed
to know where your partner is on instinct?

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:16.180
I think the thing with Azuma traumatized him
so much that he can't do that anymore.

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:20.080
- Here!
- Here!

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:24.900
That's it, that's it! Keep 'em coming!

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:30.180
Can't let them turn the tides on us.
Time to finish them off.

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:30.660
Right!

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:36.700
Guess it couldn't be that easy.

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:40.900
But the shouting keeps you from overthinking.

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:46.120
Your eyes are our key to victory.
I believe in you, Mikoto.

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:07.560
[You win]

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:14.020
You always touch this spot
when you're happy, you know.

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:18.400
I thought you were supposed to read
our opponents' minds, not mine.

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:21.000
I don't need to read anything,
you're too obvious.

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:30.420
Why did it take me so long to figure this out?

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:51.520
I'd already forgotten this feeling…!

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:57.460
That's more like it!

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:06.800
Nice one, Mikoto!

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:08.360
You've got this!

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:10.260
No way…

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:20.860
Let's go!

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:24.520
That was crazy! Insane! Epic!
Did you see that, Amano?!

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:28.880
You can't be serious!
They actually turned it around!

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:35.660
Second game won by Miyazumi and Shiratori
from Sunlight Beverage, 21-19.

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:38.560
I'm sorry, Tonozaki.

00:11:39.020 --> 00:11:41.860
Huh? What was that?

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:44.100
We're just getting to the good part!

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:46.680
Right!

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:51.000
That solves that issue.

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:56.020
The question is, will the same strategy
work in the final game?

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:03.720
Final game. Love-all. Play!

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:08.640
Man, I'm so late.

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:11.040
A client held me up.

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:13.700
Mr. Sakaki, you're beyond late!

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:15.700
They're tied and on their final game!

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:19.420
Clearly, I got my priorities wrong!

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:25.060
Nice one, Tatsuru!

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:28.140
They're doing well enough. For now…

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:40.000
Crap, not fast enough…

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.680
Damn, he still can't jump…

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:46.840
I should have been able to get that one!
What the hell is wrong with me?

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:52.120
Goddamn it…

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:05.540
How long am I gonna be relying on my partner?

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:08.480
I believe in you, Mikoto.

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:12.920
It's not that I can't jump.

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:18.880
I just convinced myself that I can't!

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:28.580
Match point, 20-19.

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:33.160
You can do it, Shiratori, Miyazumi…

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:40.020
Go, go, let's go, don't stop, don't stop, Tomari!

00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:41.880
Just one more point!

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:43.580
You've got this!

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:08.920
I'm gonna make this one count.

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:11.580
I have to make it count!

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:15.680
Please, don't freeze.

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:17.780
Please…

00:14:19.940 --> 00:14:23.240
Jump, Mikoto!

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:50.780
He jumped!

00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:56.480
Game. Match won by Miyazumi and Shiratori
from Sunlight Beverage.

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:01.420
7-21, 21-19, 21-19.

00:15:01.820 --> 00:15:04.960
Finally broken out of your shell, huh, Shiratori.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:07.840
Mikoto.

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:15.140
Nice smash.

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:20.020
Thanks.

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:39.260
I see you came to cheer us on after all.

00:15:39.780 --> 00:15:42.320
Congratulations, Miyazumi.

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:45.320
Thanks! With that,
we've made it to the quarter finals.

00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:48.540
You know, this would be the perfect time
for you to join the team.

00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:55.100
I only came because my boss told me to show
some team spirit this tournament. That's all.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:56.580
Goodbye.

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:10.440
Here's the next round of beer you ordered.

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:19.500
Damn it, I wanted to
be celebrating my own victory…

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:20.540
Ko…

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:24.700
Hey! Is it true you can't deal with crowds?

00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:27.220
Yeah, what about it?
You can laugh all you want.

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:30.320
Oh, no, I totally get it!
I had the same issue.

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:32.200
- Somehow, I doubt that.
- Somehow, I doubt that.

00:16:32.480 --> 00:16:34.920
It all happened on
a winter's day I'll never forget…

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:35.920
We didn't ask.

00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:38.630
It was my first big tournament.

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:41.780
I was stressed as balls when our coach told me…

00:16:41.780 --> 00:16:43.080
Saruhashi.

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:45.880
Just imagine they're all naked.

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:49.700
Imagine everyone in this building is naked.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:56.040
Honestly, I was shook. But I did end up winning.

00:16:57.640 --> 00:16:59.460
Well, that was a waste of time…

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:01.420
Yukei?

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:05.620
It's not like that, Tetsu!
I did my best to not imagine you naked!

00:17:05.680 --> 00:17:06.980
Wow, you stink…

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:09.880
Don't breathe in my direction…

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:18.600
You sure about this, Mikoto?

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:20.960
Don't you have something to tell Tachibana?

00:17:20.960 --> 00:17:22.960
Even if I did, that's none of your business.

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:25.660
You haven't even had a drink yet!

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:27.580
Yeah, I don't want a repeat of last itme.

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:33.520
You sure about that? You wanna miss out on
the famous Spicy Red King Crab Plum Wine?

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:37.080
Spicy Red King Crab Plum Wine…?

00:17:52.740 --> 00:17:53.660
Tonozaki!

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:00.200
Oh no, he's pissed…

00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:02.000
I, um…!

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:02.740
Listen up, kid!

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:03.800
Yes, sir!

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:06.320
Be honest, do you hate being my partner?

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:09.240
No?

00:18:09.760 --> 00:18:10.680
You mean it?

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:11.580
Yes?

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:18.200
Don't do that to me, man, I was super worried.

00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:24.560
I always sound like I'm angry,
so I worried I might be scaring you.

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:30.180
Well, if I can be honest,
I used to think you were scary.

00:18:32.800 --> 00:18:39.240
Most guys on this team are dense like me.
We won't get it unless you tell us straight.

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:41.760
We even fought a lot at first.

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:45.540
So I'm doing my best
to be honest about my feelings.

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:48.900
I want you to feel comfortable
doing the same, Tachibana.

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:54.300
This game made one thing clear for me.

00:18:55.320 --> 00:19:00.720
All this time, I worried that my partner…
that Mikoto would leave me behind.

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:02.860
That's all I could ever focus on.

00:19:03.840 --> 00:19:05.680
But worrying won't make me stronger.

00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:10.060
I want to start over in Tomari!

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:14.340
I like the sound of that.
Let's aim for the top together.

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:17.020
I'm counting on ya, partner!

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:18.990
Me too!

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:25.140
The truth is I had all the chances
in the world to talk to Mikoto.

00:19:25.780 --> 00:19:27.560
But I chose to run away instead.

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:33.180
I was so sure Mikoto
would understand me without words…

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:35.240
Miko…

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:38.160
Where the heck have you been, Azuma?

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:40.400
M-Mikoto…?

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:42.340
Azuma, I know…

00:19:42.940 --> 00:19:46.240
I know you were always there for me…

00:19:47.300 --> 00:19:51.980
You found me when I was all alone,
and invited me to the team…

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:56.640
Before you, I'd never even
been to karaoke with friends…!

00:19:57.260 --> 00:20:01.240
You took me to all these fun places…
It made me so happy…

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:04.280
You made all those
lame school events so much fun…

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:05.940
Tearful confession time…?

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:07.320
Bro, I was right there with you!

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:11.740
M-Mikoto, you can stop now,
this is really embarrassing…

00:20:13.360 --> 00:20:19.380
I… I was so scared that you might
never be able to play badminton again…

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:22.100
So I ran away.

00:20:22.100 --> 00:20:22.940
I'm sorry…!

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:26.480
I'm so sorry!

00:20:27.900 --> 00:20:29.980
But, still…

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:34.360
I'm so glad we got to play together
again today. I had so much fun!

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:37.160
I'm super grateful for everything.

00:20:39.980 --> 00:20:42.460
Tatsu, how could you get him drunk?!

00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:45.160
Sorry, he gets emotional when he's drunk.

00:20:46.040 --> 00:20:48.960
But he meant every word.

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:51.880
Not that he'll remember any of it.

00:20:55.960 --> 00:20:57.140
Go figure.

00:22:33.100 --> 00:22:34.980
You had a big ol' fall there, kid.

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:38.840
You don't need to go that hard, you know?

00:22:39.320 --> 00:22:41.260
But I didn't let it fall!

00:22:42.120 --> 00:22:43.920
You lose when the shuttle falls, right?

00:22:47.680 --> 00:22:48.860
Yeah…

00:22:49.280 --> 00:22:51.020
Yeah, you're right!

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:53.180
You're completely right!

00:22:54.280 --> 00:22:56.140
Thanks, Mikoto!

00:23:07.920 --> 00:23:11.040
I'm glad I got to be your partner in the end.
